{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"agent_message","text":"The same-prompt control changes the interpretation in a useful way. Before generation it is weak and uncertain (AUROC .657, CI [.503, .794]); after the answer it reaches .959 for lies versus same-pressure truthful answers and .896 for lies versus neutral hallucinations. So the study supports a narrow, behavior-conditioned signal—but only after showing that the conventional perfect score was entirely available from the instruction."}}
